          }
        },
        {
          "@@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are there post-study work opportunities available after graduation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, several countries have strong job markets and offer post-study work visas. Countries like Canada, Australia, and Slovakia allow international students to gain valuable work experience after completing their degrees, which can significantly boost their global career prospects."
          }
        },
        {
          "@@type": "Question",
          "name": "What factors should I consider regarding visa and immigration rules?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Every country has unique visa requirements. It is important to check if you meet the financial and documentation requirements before applying. Some countries, such as New Zealand and Slovakia, are known for having simpler and more supportive visa processes for students."
          }
        },
        {
          "@@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I consider language and culture when selecting a study destination?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Language is a major factor; decide if you prefer an English-speaking country or are willing to learn a new language. You should also consider if the local culture aligns with your lifestyle and values, as a welcoming environment is crucial for a positive student experience."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
</script>